    "notes": "Served with the r0b0tlab Qwen3.8-27B EXL3 + DFlash2 recipe (https://github.com/r0b0tlab/qwen38-exl3-dflash2, main b22a33c), which is written for a 24 GB RTX 3090 on x86. Engine: the recipe fork github.com/r0b0tlab/exllamav3 branch dflash2-pathway at 30846b8 (upstream v1.5.0 plus the DFlash2 drafter), built from source on the GB10 with torch 2.11.0+cu130, CUDA 13.0 and TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST 12.1, with the x86-only CPU sources excluded and stubbed (no GPU kernel touched). Weights: target r0b0tlab/Qwen3.8-27B-EXL3-4.00bpw at 59fa3837 and drafter r0b0tlab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-EXL3-4.00bpw at 26d05425. Engine settings follow the recipe serve script scripts/serve_openai.py: 262144-token window, paged cache of 270336 tokens, 3-bit K and V cache for both target and drafter, target recurrent history sized to the draft window, and the draft window left at the drafter default of 7 tokens (block_size 8 minus one); the generator picks the DFlash2 propose and verify path by itself from the drafter architecture. The HTTP front is not the recipe: its serve_openai.py answers non-streaming requests one at a time with no tool parsing, so the server here is TabbyAPI 53da791 (theroyallab/tabbyAPI main) with draft_mode model, max_batch_size 16, chunk_size 2048, sysmem_recurrent_cache 4096 MB, reasoning parser on and tool_format qwen3_coder, plus a one-line change that lets draft_cache_mode take the 3,3 form. The chat template is the one in the target repository, so the served default is thinking on: speed rows force thinking off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false, eval rows use the served default. No API key; the harness attached over HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8888."
